Z||000003||Daleford||01-21-2001||12:27 PM||||OK. Simply looking for the knowledgable person first. Didn't want to bore everybody with what I had. Anyway, I have a Testarossa body only,for a 7 inch stretch.  Goodshape. Maybe sold for $5995. new at one time.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-22-2001||11:46 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Daleford:<BR><B>OK. Simply looking for the knowledgable person first. Didn't want to bore everybody with what I had. Anyway, I have a Testarossa body only,for a 7 inch stretch.  Goodshape. Maybe sold for $5995. new at one time.<P>id say your not going to stand a chance of getting that. Id say if youve got everything except maybe the emblems, about $3,000-3,500. But then again since apparently no ones making Ferraris still, you might find a buyer whod pay more. I bought my stock wb 308GTB kit uninstalled with everything except a grill and emblems for $2,200 at Carlisle.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Daleford||01-22-2001||12:43 PM||||That's about what I was thinking, half of retail. I'm not greedy, maybe $2000 or less.<BR>Would I have a better chance in Daytona?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||01-22-2001||01:07 PM||||Trailering a kit car/kit car parts to Daytona from Canada in hopes of a sale may be a long drive, only to not sell it and drive it back home.  You may want to take some good quality photos of the kit car to Daytona to see if there is interest.  Maybe if you get some interest from some advertisements on the forum, there may be a buyer from the forum who will be at Daytona. Towing a trailer for 1500 miles one way is not my idea of a good time.<P>At Carlisle, it is not as far a drive from Canada, and it would have lots of kit car enthusiasts and therefore a better potential market for a sale. <P>My 2 cents.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000007||rogergarrison||01-22-2001||04:51 PM||||$2,000 is a good price. advertise it in the mall in this forum. Carlisle IS a kitcar/import show, and im pretty sure Daytona is a Fiero only show. I think youd have a better chance at Carlisle, and like lar said, it isnt too far to trailer. I wouldnt mind it myself except Im not for the frame stretching part.||||reg||1
